From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lkshrk <dev@harke.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:07:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] Rebase the omp fork onto v0.35.1

Upstream v0.35.1 keeps self-defined MCP server names that contain a
slash as the config key in every target (#3493). The omp adapter now
passes the server info to the key lookup as the other adapters do, and
returns False on any lookup error, which the new cross-target test
requires.

The fork's remount fix for deployment receipts is dropped: upstream
fixed the same report in #3439 with a stricter rebind check.

The native hook cleanup in uninstall and the previous-lockfile hash
lookup in integrate_package_primitives move into helpers, keeping both
functions inside the lint limits after the merge. drift.py and
manifest_reconcile.py get per-file budgets for the fork's additions.

Version 0.35.1+omni.1.
